From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: cmake: set HAVE_SSIZE_T

The CMake build checks the size of ssize_t but never sets HAVE_SSIZE_T, so
config.h always defines ssize_t as intptr_t. Where ssize_t is long and
intptr_t is int (AArch64 ILP32), the C library's typedefs then conflict.

---
--- a/cmake/SndFileChecks.cmake
+++ b/cmake/SndFileChecks.cmake
@@ -95,6 +95,8 @@
 check_type_size (long				SIZEOF_LONG)
 check_type_size (long\ long			SIZEOF_LONG_LONG)
 check_type_size (ssize_t			SIZEOF_SSIZE_T)
+# config.h defines ssize_t as intptr_t without this; they differ on AArch64 ILP32
+set (HAVE_SSIZE_T ${HAVE_SIZEOF_SSIZE_T})
 check_type_size (wchar_t			SIZEOF_WCHAR_T)
 
 # Never used
